{{- /*
  Denial page. Renders web.DeniedView: a constant message stating why
  the request was refused — never the identity, never probe detail.
*/ -}}
{{template "page-head" "denied"}}
{{template "shell-open" .Shell}}
  <header>
    <div class="header-bar">
      <h1>pgConsole</h1>
    </div>
  </header>
    {{- /* The refusal states the reason, what the reader holds, and the
           whole ladder — so someone who has been refused can tell what
           to ask for instead of guessing. The level is display only and
           is already in the top bar; nothing here is an identity. */}}
    <section class="panel denied">
      <h2>Not available at your level</h2>
      <p class="denied-reason">{{.Message}}.</p>
      {{- if .Level}}
      <p class="denied-level">The proxy asserted the <strong>{{.Level}}</strong> level for this request.</p>
      {{- else}}
      <p class="denied-level">The proxy asserted <strong>no level</strong> for this request, so the console admits it to nothing. Reaching the console is not authorization: the level decides every screen.</p>
      {{- end}}
      <dl class="facts">
        <dt>view</dt>
        <dd>The overviews — cluster, backups, databases and poolers — and the two metrics screens.</dd>
        <dt>poweruser</dt>
        <dd>Everything the console reads: the object inventories, the pod rosters and their detail, the object history, the repository evidence, and the bounded log tails.</dd>
        <dt>dba</dt>
        <dd>Everything above, plus the four day-2 operations and the access-request review panel.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p class="origin">Levels are asserted by the proxy in front of this console, not decided here. Ask whoever operates that proxy; the console has no way to grant one.</p>
    </section>
{{template "shell-close"}}
